\ Spitfire: the clouds. Cumulus stand on a common base, each a cluster of
\ spheres in a 3 km square of the sky chosen by a hash of the square's
\ position, so the same clouds are there whenever the aircraft returns; the
\ mission sets the share of squares that hold one and the base's height.
\ The spheres within 15 km of the aircraft are gathered again only when it
\ crosses into another square. Each frame every sphere in view is drawn as
\ a filled disc, the upper spheres lighter than the lower, faded into the
\ sky with distance; the discs and the bombers are drawn together from the
\ farthest to the nearest, so a bomber in front of a cloud shows and one
\ behind it is hidden. With the eye inside a sphere the whole view is the
\ cloud's colour, and only the instruments tell which way is up.

3000 constant cloud-square
5 constant cloud-reach

variable cloud-cover
0 to cloud-cover
variable cloud-base
1500 to cloud-base
variable cloud-squares
{ } to cloud-squares
variable cloud-square-at
[ null null ] to cloud-square-at
variable cloud-centres
0 4 0-matrix to cloud-centres
variable cloud-radii
0 1 0-matrix to cloud-radii
variable cloud-shades
0 1 0-matrix to cloud-shades
variable in-cloud
false to in-cloud

\ the weather's clouds: the share of squares holding one and the height of their base; the clouds gathered before are forgotten
: use-clouds ( cover base -- )
	| cover base ^cloud-cover ^cloud-base ^cloud-squares ^cloud-square-at |
	cover to cloud-cover
	base to cloud-base
	{ } to cloud-squares
	[ null null ] to cloud-square-at ;

\ one square's cloud as spheres [ x y z radius shade ], the shade 0 at the base and near 1 at the top; none when the hash leaves the square clear
: square-cloud ( column row -- spheres )
	| column row |
	column 7.31 * row 13.17 * + 101 + to seed
	seed hash-fraction cloud-cover >= if [ ] exit then
	column 0.2 + seed 1.1 + hash-fraction 0.6 * + cloud-square * to x
	row 0.2 + seed 2.3 + hash-fraction 0.6 * + cloud-square * to z
	250 seed 3.7 + hash-fraction 450 * + to size
	5 seed 4.9 + hash-fraction 4 * truncate + to n-spheres
	[ 0 n-spheres 1 do k
		seed k 1.3 * + 5.1 + to puff
		size 0.45 puff hash-fraction 0.35 * + * to radius
		puff 0.7 + hash-fraction 0.5 - 2.2 * size * to across
		puff 1.9 + hash-fraction 0.5 - 1.4 * size * to along
		puff 2.6 + hash-fraction 0.6 * size * to rise
		[ x across + cloud-base radius 0.5 * + rise + z along + radius rise size 0.6 * / ]
	loop ] ;

\ the clouds near a point: their spheres' centres, radii and shades as columns, gathered when the point crosses into another square
: refresh-clouds ( position -- )
	| position ^cloud-squares ^cloud-square-at ^cloud-centres ^cloud-radii ^cloud-shades |
	position first cloud-square / round-down to column
	position 2 @i cloud-square / round-down to row
	cloud-square-at [ column row ] = if exit then
	[ column row ] to cloud-square-at
	[ ] to near-spheres
	column cloud-reach - column cloud-reach + 1 + 1 do c
		row cloud-reach - row cloud-reach + 1 + 1 do r
			c r "{1}/{0}" format string>symbol to key
			cloud-squares key has? not if
				cloud-squares c r square-cloud key ! drop
			then
			near-spheres cloud-squares key @ concat to near-spheres
		loop
	loop
	near-spheres size to n-spheres
	n-spheres 0 = if
		0 4 0-matrix to cloud-centres
		0 1 0-matrix to cloud-radii
		0 1 0-matrix to cloud-shades
		exit
	then
	near-spheres ( sphere | [ sphere first sphere second sphere 2 @i 1 ] ) map flatten n-spheres 4 matrix to cloud-centres
	near-spheres ( sphere | sphere 3 @i ) map vector to cloud-radii
	near-spheres ( sphere | sphere 4 @i ) map vector to cloud-shades ;

\ a disc of cloud in the view: a small one by the window's own disc, a large one in rows cut to the view
: cloud-disc ( x y radius colour -- )
	| x y radius colour |
	radius 40 < if x y radius colour fill-disc exit then
	y radius - 0 max2 round to top
	y radius + view-height min2 round to bottom
	top bottom 2 do row
		radius sq row 1 + y - sq - to room
		room 0 > if
			room sqrt to half
			x half - 0 max2 round to left
			x half + view-width min2 round to right
			right left > if left row right left - 2 colour fill-span then
		then
	loop ;

\ the clouds and the raid, from the farthest to the nearest, each sphere in view a disc; the whole view the cloud's colour when the eye is inside a sphere
: draw-sky ( -- )
	| ^in-cloud |
	false to in-cloud
	cloud-radii num-elements to n-spheres
	[ ] to items
	n-spheres 0 > if
		cloud-centres camera matmul to viewed
		viewed 0 @j to across
		viewed 1 @j to rising
		viewed 2 @j to ahead
		across sq rising sq + ahead sq + to distance-squared
		distance-squared cloud-radii sq < sum 0 > to in-cloud
		ahead near-plane > to in-front
		ahead in-front * 1 in-front - + to safe-ahead
		focal-length across * safe-ahead / view-centre-x + to xs
		view-centre-y focal-length rising * safe-ahead / - to ys
		focal-length cloud-radii * safe-ahead / to rs
		in-front
		xs rs + 0 > *
		xs rs - view-width < *
		ys rs + 0 > *
		ys rs - view-height < *
		distance-squared sqrt cloud-radii - visibility < *
		where to shown
		0 shown num-elements 1 do k
			shown k @e to i
			items [ ahead i @e 0 i ] add-last! drop
		loop
	then
	0 bombers size 1 do k
		bombers k @i to bomber
		bomber@position eye@position v- eye@attitude@forward v-dot to depth
		items [ depth 1 k ] add-last! drop
	loop
	items ( item | item first negate ) sort-by to ordered
	0 ordered size 1 do k
		ordered k @i spread to index to kind to depth
		kind 1 = if
			bombers index @i draw-bomber
		else
			cloud-top-colour cloud-base-colour cloud-shades index @e blended to colour
			colour sky-colour distance-squared index @e sqrt depth-light blended to colour
			xs index @e ys index @e rs index @e colour cloud-disc
		then
	loop
	in-cloud if 0 0 view-width view-height cloud-top-colour cloud-base-colour 0.6 blended fill-span then ;
